# Source of truth for the runtime dependencies. requirements.txt is GENERATED
# from this file and pins every package, including transitive ones — edit this
# file, never that one, then regenerate:
#
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --universal --python-version 3.12 -o requirements.txt
#   uv pip compile requirements-dev.in --universal --python-version 3.12 -c requirements.txt -o requirements-dev.txt
#
# --universal keeps the environment markers, so one lock serves Linux (CI and
# Vercel) and Windows (local) — uvloop stays excluded on win32, colorama stays
# included. --python-version 3.12 matches .python-version and CI; resolving on
# the local 3.14 would pin versions production never sees.
#
# On a machine whose antivirus intercepts HTTPS (Norton, here), uv rejects the
# substituted certificate — add --native-tls to read the OS trust store. Same
# root cause as api/_src/dev_loop.py.
